# L §5.14.3 (round 12): "for k: the period the amount is for ... flows(x, span, for k) reads only instances for period
# k. A movement with no for (of a move without one, a pad, an observation that fulfils nothing) is for no period, and ,
# for k leaves it out; an observation that fulfils an instance is for the instance's period." Over Jan-Apr: wage[m] is
# for m (100.00 PLN each), bonus has no for, April is covered by a statement: bank[r1] (110.00) fulfils wage[2026-04],
# bank[r2] (7.00) fulfils nothing. for 2026-03: 100.00; for 2026-04: 110.00; all: 3 x 100 + 100 + 110 + 7 = 517.00.
# (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.14.3, writer 5's T-69.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int
input bday: date

move wage[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  for m
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

move bonus: transfers
  on bday
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  dom = 10
  bday = 2026-03-15
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-04
  known 2026-05-01
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-04-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 110.00 PLN, fulfils: wage[2026-04]) "l1"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-04-20, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 7.00 PLN) "l2"

ask q: flows(konto, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-04-30, for 2026-03), flows(konto, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-04-30, for 2026-04), flows(konto, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-04-30)
=== expect
q: (100.00 PLN, 110.00 PLN, 517.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: bonus
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: wage[2026-03]
  cut 2026-12-31
